  "response": "To configure LlamaIndex to use a local Ollama LLM and a Hugging Face embedding model globally, you need to set these models in the `Settings` object. This configuration ensures that OpenAI services are not contacted. Here's how you can do it:\n\n1. **Install the necessary packages**:\n   - Ensure you have `llama-index-llms-ollama` for the Ollama integration.\n   - Ensure you have `llama-index-embeddings-openai` for using Hugging Face embeddings.\n\n2. **Set up the local Ollama LLM**:\n   - Use the `Ollama` class from `llama_index.llms.ollama` to configure your local Ollama model.\n\n3. **Set up the global Hugging Face embedding model**:\n   - Use the `HuggingFaceEmbedding` class from `llama_index.embeddings.huggingface`.\n\n4. **Configure the `Settings` object**:\n   - Set the `llm` and `embed_model` in the `Settings` object.\n\nHere is a code example to achieve this:\n\n```python\nfrom llama_index.llms.ollama import Ollama\nfrom llama_index.embeddings.huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbedding\nfrom llama_index.core import Settings\n\n# Configure the local Ollama LLM\nllm = Ollama(\n    model=\"llama3.3\",  # Specify the model you want to use\n    request_timeout=60.0,\n    context_window=8000,  # Optional: Adjust based on your memory constraints\n)\n\n# Configure the global Hugging Face embedding model\nSettings.embed_model = HuggingFaceEmbedding()\n\n# Set the LLM in Settings\nSettings.llm = llm\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- **Ollama Configuration**: The `Ollama` class is used to configure the local LLM. You specify the model and optional parameters like `request_timeout` and `context_window`.\n- **Hugging Face Embedding**: The `HuggingFaceEmbedding` class is set as the global embedding model in `Settings.embed_model`.\n- **Global Settings**: By setting `Settings.llm` and `Settings.embed_model`, you ensure that these configurations are used globally across LlamaIndex, preventing any calls to OpenAI services.\n\nThis setup allows you to run LlamaIndex entirely locally with the specified models.\n\n**References**:\n- \"Running LlamaIndex fully locally\" [1] and \"Using local models\" [4] provide context on running LlamaIndex locally.\n- \"Available local LLM integrations\" [2] lists the Ollama integration.\n- \"Usage Pattern\" [6] explains setting global embedding models.\n- \"Using a local LLM\" [7] details configuring a local Ollama model.",
